    "/repos/{owner}/{repo}/archives/{format}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Prepares the files of a branch, tag or commit as a tar.gz or zip archive and gives its link (\`download_url\`, GitHub's tarball or zipball route; the same token works). A large archive is built in the background: \`state\` is \`building\` until it is \`ready\`; ask again, or fetch the link, which answers 202 until then. Archives hold 1 GiB of files at most, each file 24 MiB at most, a zip 65,535 entries.",
